<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">layer_sequence_play</span></h1>
<p>With this function you can start the playback of the given sequence. You supply the sequence element ID as returned by <span class="inline3_func"><a href="layer_sequence_create.htm">layer_sequence_create</a></span> or by one of the <a href="../General_Layer_Functions/General_Layer_Functions.htm">layer element functions</a> and the function will play the sequence, which you can then pause if required using the function <span class="inline3_func"><a href="layer_sequence_pause.htm">layer_sequence_pause</a></span>.<b></b></p>
<div data-conref="../../../../../assets/snippets/Note_Instances_In_Sequence_Shouldnt_Update_Transform_Vars.hts">
<p class="note"><b><span data-conref="../../../../../assets/snippets/Tag_important.hts"><span class="important">IMPORTANT</span></span> </b>If your sequence has any instances in it, these instances shouldn&#39;t change their <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Sprites/Sprite_Instance_Variables/image_xscale.htm">image_xscale</a></span>  / <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Sprites/Sprite_Instance_Variables/image_yscale.htm">image_yscale</a></span> / <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Sprites/Sprite_Instance_Variables/image_angle.htm">image_angle</a></span> / <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Instances/Instance_Variables/x.htm">x</a></span> / <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Instances/Instance_Variables/y.htm">y</a></span> variables as they will be overwritten when the sequence updates each step after starting to be played. You can check <span class="inline2"><a href="../../Sequences/in_sequence.htm">in_sequence</a></span> and only update the properties of such an instance when this variable is <span class="inline2">false</span>.</p>
</div>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">layer_sequence_play</span>(sequence_element_id)</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>sequence_element_id</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_ID_Element_Sequence"><a target="_blank" href="layer_sequence_create.htm">Sequence Element ID</a></span></td>
<td>The unique ID value of the sequence element to target</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Void">N/A</span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">if (keyboard_check_pressed(ord(&quot;P&quot;)))<br/>
{<br/>
    global.Pause = !global.Pause;<br/>
    var a = layer_get_all_elements(layer);<br/>
    for (var i = 0; i &lt; array_length(a); i++;)<br/>
    {<br/>
        if (layer_get_element_type(a[i]) == layerelementtype_sequence)<br/>
        {<br/>
            if (global.Pause)<br/>
            {<br/>
                layer_sequence_pause(a[i]);<br/>
            }<br/>
            else<br/>
            {<br/>
                layer_sequence_play(a[i]);<br/>
            }<br/>
        }<br/>
    }<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code checks to see if the game has been paused or not when a key is pressed. If the game is paused, then it loops through all sequence elements on the current layer (the layer of the calling instance) and pauses their playback, and if the game is not paused, then the loop will start their playback again.</p>
